{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>The dia.</b> A general term for two species, namely dia and dayah, like \"the bird\" that is not split into \"turtledove and young pigeon.\" And indeed the copyists were right who said that ra'ah is dia, and the argument of Rabbi Yonah, who said: How is it possible to say 'Beware the lion and the cat,' falls away. Some say: nesher is from our ashur; peres is from \"not spare from hunger\"; azniyah is from oz, and the nun is added, and it is called akba; and dia is from \"as the nesher swoops\"; and ayah is so called because its habit is to dwell on known islands."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The verse 'ואת הצפור לא תבכיר' (Deut 22:6) is quoted loosely; the phrase 'תור וגוזל' is not a direct biblical quote but Ibn Ezra's illustration. Rabbi Yonah's phrase 'האריה והליש' likely echoes his lost commentary; the sense seems to be an analogy about listing two names for one creature. 'עקב״א' and 'אשורנו' are left as transliterated since their identification is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:29.626264188Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}